ompose-up.sh is named `compose-mcp-1` (compose default), which does not match the `rebar-mcp-*` pattern the plan says the retire sweep and MCP_RELEASES_CAP count over. The first deploy after boot, and retirement of that original compose-started container, are unspecified — the sweep may never see/reclaim it and the cap accounting may be off by one.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4167814b2d053931","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 6 ('managed `rebar-mcp-*` count exceeds MCP_RELEASES_CAP'); Retire-when-idle sweep","norm_id":"n3f66ee720dcdee2e","priority":0.603,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["First mcp deploy after a box boot: nginx flips from the compose-started 8091 container to a new rebar-mcp-<sha> on 8092, but the old compose-mcp-1 is never enumerated by the rebar-mcp-* sweep and lingers holding port 8091 / memory"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify how the second (green) MCP container is launched on MCP_PORT_B while the blue one keeps 8091 — the exact `docker run`/compose-override invocation and how it inherits the compose service's env_file, REBAR_MCP_*/REBAR_OPCERT_* env, the two `:ro` secret bind-mounts, stop_grace_period, and journald logging — since `docker compose up mcp` publishes only the single fixed 8091 host port.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.0,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Start a NEW container alongside old ... on the OTHER port of the A/B pair (MCP_PORT_A=8091/MCP_PORT_B=8092, container port fixed 8091)'","docker-compose.yml mcp: `ports: - \"127.0.0.1:8091:8091\"` and `environment: REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PORT: \"8091\"` — a single fixed published host port","Plan uses `docker compose build mcp` for the IMAGE only and manages bespoke `rebar-mcp-*` containers, but the launch invocation for the second instance is unspecified","The mcp service carries 8 env vars, env_file: .env, two `:ro` secret bind-mounts (mcp-static-tokens.json, opcert-ed25519-key), and stop_grace_period 1260s that a bespoke second container must reproduce to boot fail-closed"],"finding":"The plan asserts a blue-green A/B port pair (start a NEW container on MCP_PORT_B=8092 while the OLD serves 8091), but the compose `mcp` service publishes a single fixed host port (127.0.0.1:8091:8091) and hardcodes REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8091; the plan never states the mechanism by which a second live container is started on 8092 nor how it inherits the compose service's env_file / REBAR_MCP_* + REBAR_OPCERT_* env / read-only secret bind-mounts / stop_grace_period. `docker compose up mcp` (used elsewhere) cannot start a second instance on a different host port and would collide on 8091.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb9d75a5e65f1970b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach steps 3 & 6; docker-compose.yml mcp service (ports 127.0.0.1:8091:8091, REBAR_MCP_HTTP_PORT=8091)","norm_id":"n6e3dc3c838e422fe","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["First blue-green flip: the second container must bind 8092 host-side while the container listens on 8091; a `docker compose up mcp` would either recreate the single service (killing the in-flight op the plan exists to protect) or collide on 8091","A bespoke `docker run` that omits any REBAR_MCP_AUTH_* / secret mount / TLS-at-edge ack boots into McpStartupError or serves /mcp unauthenticated"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"high"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify HOW the parallel `rebar-mcp-<sha>` container is launched given the compose `mcp` service pins `127.0.0.1:8091:8091` with no container_name — state the `docker run` (or compose-override) invocation and how the compose-declared `.env`/env_file, REBAR_MCP_* env, the two `:ro` secret bind-mounts, and stop_grace_period=1260s are reproduced on the standalone container so the second instance actually starts on the other port with identical config.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.131,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["docker-compose.yml:357-360 pins `ports: - \"127.0.0.1:8091:8091\"` for the `mcp` service","docker-compose.yml `mcp` service has NO `container_name` (search returned no matches) → compose names it `compose-mcp-1`, a single service instance","docker-compose.yml:330-373 declares env_file `.env`, REBAR_MCP_* env, and two `:ro` secret bind-mounts (mcp-static-tokens.json, opcert-ed25519-key) plus stop_grace_period:1260s — all of which a raw `docker run` would have to replicate","ADR 0104 §2 line 66 says 'Start a new `rebar-mcp` container alongside the old one' — the `rebar-mcp-<sha>` naming the plan uses implies `docker run`, not `docker compose up`, but the plan never states this"],"finding":"The A/B two-container overlap cannot be achieved with `docker compose up mcp`: the compose `mcp` service pins `127.0.0.1:8091:8091` and has no container_name, so compose runs ONE container on 8091 and `up` recreates (kills) it rather than starting a second on 8092. The plan builds via `docker compose build mcp` but never specifies the run mechanism for the parallel container, nor how the compose-declared env_file/.env, the two read-only secret bind-mounts, the REBAR_MCP_* environment, and stop_grace_period=1260s are reproduced on that standalone container.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f70c31624212c9336","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 & 3 ('Build ... docker compose build mcp'; 'Start a NEW container alongside old ... on the OTHER port of the A/B pair'; MCP_PORT_A=8091/MCP_PORT_B=8092, container port fixed 8091)","norm_id":"n1fe66b9a7cbf76ce","priority":0.469,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Implementer wires `docker compose up mcp` for the second container and it kills the live one (defeating one-in/one-out) or fails to bind 8092","Implementer uses `docker run` but omits a secret bind-mount or env var, so the new container fails auth/opcert startup and the deploy loops on mcp-unhealthy"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the first-deploy/bootstrap behavior when the installed nginx include is absent: which A/B port to select as the initial live port, that no old container exists to retire, and that the missing-backup path is a non-error.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"current live port is read back from the installed nginx include\"","step 5 backs up 'the installed include' assuming it exists","no bootstrap case described for the first deploy where no include/live container exists"],"finding":"The plan reads the current live port back from the installed nginx include but does not specify behavior when that include is absent (first-ever mcp deploy / fresh box), where there is no live port to read.","group_criteria":null,"group_id